From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 05:08:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: sound: qcom,sm8250: allow a codec master clock
 on the card

The comma 3X's MAX98089 codec is programmed from userspace and has no
kernel driver, so nothing would enable the master clock it runs from.
Allow the sound card to take that clock as an optional "mclk", which
the sdm845 machine driver then keeps enabled while the card is bound.

This is local to AGNOS, like the sdm845 patch that uses it. Upstream,
the codec would be described as a device that owns its own MCLK.

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml
index 1536fcd96d..59765f7b2d 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml
@@ -55,6 +55,15 @@ properties:
           - qcom,sm8450-sndcard
           - qcom,x1e80100-sndcard
 
+  clocks:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      Master clock of a codec that is not described as a device, kept
+      enabled while the card is bound.
+
+  clock-names:
+    const: mclk
+
   audio-routing:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/non-unique-string-array
     description:
